# 3. UI/UX DESIGN SYSTEM

## 3.1 Visual Direction

Use the provided mockup image as the primary visual reference.

The design should feel like a premium artisan bakery brand: elegant, warm, modern, editorial, professional, and inviting.

The application must combine luxury bakery photography with clean layouts, refined typography, generous whitespace, and intuitive interactions.

Avoid generic dashboard templates, oversized solid-color hero sections, excessive gradients, cluttered layouts, and inconsistent components.

## 3.2 Exact Color Theme

Use the following color palette consistently throughout the entire application.

| Purpose            | Color               | Hex Code |
| ------------------ | ------------------- | -------- |
| Main background    | Warm ivory          | #FAF7F2  |
| Card background    | Pure white          | #FFFFFF  |
| Primary brand      | Deep burgundy       | #762F3D  |
| Primary hover      | Dark burgundy       | #5F2030  |
| Secondary accent   | Muted gold          | #C5A46D  |
| Soft blush         | Pale blush          | #F3E6DF  |
| Primary text       | Dark brown-charcoal | #302725  |
| Secondary text     | Muted warm gray     | #80736F  |
| Borders            | Warm light gray     | #E8E0D9  |
| Success background | Soft sage green     | #E2F0E4  |
| Success text       | Dark green          | #326B45  |
| Warning background | Pale amber          | #FFF0D5  |
| Error background   | Pale rose           | #FBE5E5  |
| Error text         | Dark red            | #A33242  |

These colors establish the required visual direction. Use the burgundy and gold tones consistently and do not introduce unrelated bright accent colors.

### Color Distribution

* 65–75% warm ivory and white surfaces.
* 10–15% photography and image content.
* 5–10% burgundy accents.
* Remaining space for muted gold, blush, borders, and status colors.

Do not use burgundy as the background for every section.

The public storefront should primarily use ivory and white backgrounds. Burgundy should emphasize buttons, selected navigation items, important headings, and key actions.

## 3.3 Typography

Use:

* **Playfair Display** for elegant headings.
* **Inter** for body text, buttons, forms, tables, and dashboard elements.

Typography requirements:

* Clear heading hierarchy.
* Comfortable reading sizes.
* Consistent font weights.
* Proper line heights.
* Responsive font scaling.
* No excessively large headings that overwhelm the interface.

Load fonts reliably and provide fallback fonts.

## 3.4 Layout and Components

Use:

* Consistent content widths.
* Generous but efficient spacing.
* Rounded corners between 10px and 16px for most cards.
* Subtle, realistic shadows.
* Fine, warm-toned borders.
* High-quality photography.
* Consistent iconography.
* Clear primary and secondary actions.
* Well-designed form controls.
* Consistent status badges.

Use Lucide icons or another consistent icon library.

Avoid excessive glassmorphism. This project should prioritize the warm, refined bakery aesthetic shown in the reference.

## 3.5 Buttons

Primary buttons:

* Burgundy background.
* White text.
* Subtle hover transition.
* Clear disabled state.
* Consistent height and padding.

Secondary buttons:

* White or transparent background.
* Burgundy text or border.

Tertiary actions:

* Simple text buttons or icon buttons with accessible labels.

Destructive actions must use an appropriate error color and confirmation where necessary.

## 3.6 Photography

Use attractive, high-quality images of real bakery products.

Images should include:

* Chocolate fudge cakes.
* Red velvet cakes.
* Vanilla cupcakes.
* Brownies.
* Croissants.
* Cookies.
* Custom wedding cakes.
* Bakery interiors and cake decorations.

Use consistent aspect ratios and proper image cropping.

Use locally stored assets or reliable image sources. Do not depend on arbitrary external image URLs that may stop working.

If no suitable image is available, use a graceful placeholder rather than a broken image.

## 3.7 Responsive Design

Support:

* Mobile: 360px–767px.
* Tablet: 768px–1023px.
* Desktop: 1024px and above.
* Large desktop: 1440px and above.

Requirements:

* No horizontal overflow.
* Responsive navigation.
* Mobile-friendly forms.
* Properly sized product cards.
* Touch-friendly buttons.
* Responsive charts and tables.
* Collapsible sidebars.
* Adaptive dashboard grids.
* Mobile-friendly checkout and POS layouts.

