# 4. USER ROLES AND PERMISSIONS

The application must support the following roles.

## 4.1 Guest

A guest can:

* Browse the homepage.
* View products and categories.
* Search and filter products.
* View product details.
* Configure a custom cake request.
* Register or sign in.
* Access public business information.

Guests must sign in before accessing protected customer features or submitting orders that require an account.

## 4.2 Customer

Customers can:

* Manage their profiles.
* Browse and purchase products.
* Add products to a cart.
* Place orders.
* Request custom cakes.
* Select delivery or pickup where available.
* View order history.
* Track order progress.
* View payment information.
* Save delivery addresses.
* Cancel eligible orders according to business rules.
* Receive notifications about order updates.

Customers must never access internal management screens or other customers' private information.

## 4.3 Admin / Owner

The owner has complete authorized access to:

* Dashboard.
* Orders.
* Custom cake orders.
* Products and categories.
* Inventory.
* Production.
* Customers.
* Staff.
* Suppliers.
* Deliveries.
* Expenses.
* Reports.
* Payments.
* Settings.
* Audit logs.

The owner can manage user roles and permissions.

## 4.4 Manager

The manager can:

* View operational dashboards.
* Manage orders.
* Manage custom cake requests.
* Manage products.
* Coordinate production.
* Manage customers.
* Review inventory.
* Manage assigned operational tasks.
* View authorized reports.

The manager must not automatically receive permission to change owner accounts or sensitive system settings.

## 4.5 Cashier

The cashier can:

* Access the POS.
* Search products.
* Add items to a cart.
* Create walk-in orders.
* Select existing customers or register walk-in customer details.
* Apply authorized discounts.
* Record supported payment methods.
* Print or download receipts.
* View permitted order information.
* Process eligible refunds only if authorized.

The cashier must not access staff administration, unrestricted financial reports, or system configuration.

## 4.6 Baker

The baker can:

* View assigned production tasks.
* View cake specifications.
* Review custom cake reference images.
* See preparation deadlines.
* Update production status.
* Add production notes.
* Mark tasks as completed.
* View relevant ingredient availability.

The baker cannot access unrelated customer data, staff permissions, or financial reports.

## 4.7 Inventory Manager

The inventory manager can:

* Manage ingredients.
* Manage stock quantities.
* Record purchases.
* Manage suppliers.
* Record stock adjustments.
* Monitor low-stock alerts.
* Track ingredient usage.
* View inventory reports.

The inventory manager cannot change owner permissions or access unrestricted financial data.

## 4.8 Delivery Staff

Delivery staff can:

* View assigned deliveries.
* View necessary customer contact and delivery details.
* View delivery instructions.
* Update delivery status.
* Record delivery attempts.
* Confirm successful delivery.

Delivery staff must not access unrelated customers, staff accounts, or internal financial reports.

## 4.9 Permission Enforcement

Implement role-based access control on both frontend and backend.

Hiding a button is not sufficient security.

Every protected API must verify the authenticated user's permissions.

Use reusable authorization middleware and a centralized permission strategy.

